Here's the approach: bypass `IFormFile` and read the multipart body directly using `MultipartReader`, streaming each section to disk.

**1. Disable request size limits**

```csharp
// Program.cs
builder.WebApplication.MapPost("/upload", HandleUpload)
    .DisableAntiforgery()
    .WithMetadata(new RequestSizeLimitAttribute(2L * 1024 * 1024 * 1024)); // 2 GB
```

Also in `Program.cs` (or `appsettings.json` for Kestrel):

```csharp
builder.WebHost.ConfigureKestrel(o =>
{
    o.Limits.MaxRequestBodySize = 2L * 1024 * 1024 * 1024;
});
```

**2. Stream the multipart body to disk**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities;
using Microsoft.Net.Http.Headers;

static async Task<IResult> HandleUpload(HttpRequest request)
{
    if (!request.HasFormContentType ||
        !MediaTypeHeaderValue.TryParse(request.ContentType, out var mt) ||
        string.IsNullOrEmpty(mt.Boundary.Value))
    {
        return Results.BadRequest("Expected a multipart request.");
    }

    var boundary = HeaderUtilities.RemoveQuotes(mt.Boundary).Value!;
    var reader = new MultipartReader(boundary, request.Body);

    MultipartSection? section;
    while ((section = await reader.ReadNextSectionAsync()) != null)
    {
        if (!ContentDispositionHeaderValue.TryParse(section.ContentDisposition, out var cd) ||
            !cd.IsFileDisposition())
        {
            continue; // skip non-file fields
        }

        var trustedName = Path.GetRandomFileName(); // avoid path traversal
        var savePath = Path.Combine(Path.GetTempPath(), trustedName);

        await using var fs = new FileStream(
            savePath, FileMode.Create, FileAccess.Write, FileShare.None,
            bufferSize: 81920, useAsync: true);

        await section.Body.CopyToAsync(fs);
    }

    return Results.Ok("Upload complete.");
}
```

**Key points:**

| Concern | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| Memory pressure | `MultipartReader` streams section-by-section; never buffers the full file |
| Default 30 MB limit | Override with `MaxRequestBodySize` on Kestrel + `[RequestSizeLimit]` metadata |
| Model binding | Skip `[FromForm]`/`IFormFile` entirely—they buffer to memory or a temp file managed by the framework |
| Security | Use `Path.GetRandomFileName()` instead of the client-supplied filename to prevent path traversal |

**3. Optional: disable form value buffering globally**

```csharp
builder.Services.Configure<FormOptions>(o =>
{
    o.MultipartBodyLengthLimit = 2L * 1024 * 1024 * 1024;
    o.BufferBody = false;
});
```

This ensures nothing in the pipeline accidentally buffers the body even if middleware reads `Request.Form`.
